__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
docs/OBSERVATION.md
docs/AGENT_OBS.md
*.log
.DS_Store
runs/
eval_videos/

# Sprite PNGs are extracted game assets (Supercell IP) -- keep the folder structure and README
# tracked, not the images themselves. See brawl_sim/render/assets/README.md.
brawl_sim/render/assets/**/*.png
# Screen captures and recorded clips of a live match are extracted game assets (Supercell IP),
# the same rule as the sprite PNGs above. Ignored BY EXTENSION rather than by directory, so the
# folder structure, the READMEs, and -- critically -- the hand-authored ground truth that lives
# alongside the footage (label CSVs, *.truth.json, *.grid.csv) all stay tracked. Those are your
# annotations, not Supercell's pixels, and they are what the regression fixtures actually assert
# against. See Terrain_Perception_Build_Plan.md Phase 0.
brawl_vision/data/frames/**/*.png
brawl_vision/data/frames/**/*.jpg
brawl_vision/data/frames/**/*.jpeg
tests/fixtures/vision/**/*.png
tests/fixtures/vision/**/*.jpg
tests/fixtures/vision/**/*.jpeg
tests/fixtures/vision/**/*.mp4
tests/fixtures/vision/**/*.mkv

# Third-party detector weights (brawl_vision/object_detection). Fetched, not committed: 10.6 MB
# of somebody else's AGPL-licensed model from a repo with no releases and no licence file. The
# NOTICE.md beside them -- provenance, SHA-256, class lists, the licence question -- IS tracked,
# and `python scripts/vision_fetch_detector.py` puts the blobs back. Same split as data/ above:
# structure and documentation tracked, opaque payload not.
brawl_vision/object_detection/weights/*.onnx
brawl_vision/object_detection/weights/*.pt
brawl_vision/object_detection/weights/*.part
brawl_vision/data/training_videos/**

# Projectile training set (brawl_vision/object_detection/projectile_detection). The CVAT export is
# 906 MB and `dataset/` is 869 MB of the same bytes, unpacked by train.py on first run; the COCO
# yolo26n.pt is 5.3 MB of Ultralytics' AGPL-licensed weights. `runs/` is covered by the rule at the
# top of this file. Code and docstrings tracked, payload not -- same split as the two blocks above.
brawl_vision/object_detection/projectile_detection/*.zip
brawl_vision/object_detection/projectile_detection/dataset/
brawl_vision/object_detection/projectile_detection/*.pt

# Ultralytics' AMP check downloads a throwaway yolo26n.pt to ./weights on the first train run.
# Not ours, not used for training, recreated on demand.
/weights/

# graphify (local knowledge graph for Claude Code). Kept off the repo entirely: the graph and its
# build sidecars live in graphify-out/, and `graphify claude install` writes its always-on section
# to CLAUDE.md and its PreToolUse hooks (absolute exe paths, machine-specific) to
# .claude/settings.json. Un-ignore those two if the project ever needs a shared CLAUDE.md or
# settings.json. graphify honours this file when it scans, so everything ignored here stays out
# of the graph as well.
graphify-out/
CLAUDE.md
.claude/settings.json

Terrain_Perception_Build_Plan.md
TRAINING.md
BRAWL_SIM_BUILD_PLAN.md
CONVENTIONS.md
bot_overhaul.md
EDGAR_HERO_PLAN.md
